contentText:
A judge scheduled a new trial date in the long-running child sexual assault lawsuit against Aerosmith frontman Steven Tyler and said he was open to revisiting the scope of the case.

In a Monday (Nov. 9) court ruling, obtained by Billboard , the judge set a May 2027 trial for Julia Misley’s claims that Tyler sexually &#8220;groomed&#8221; her as a teenager in the 1970s — and then essentially admitted it by writing in a memoir that he &#8220;almost took a teen bride.&#8221; The order came from Los Angeles Judge Lawrence P. Riff, the sixth judge who has taken on the slow-moving civil case since 2022.

